<H1 align="center">Hamiltonian Systems</H1>

<h3>Organizer</h3>
<p>
<ADDRESS>
Alexander Bruno
(<a href="mailto:bruno@applmat.msk.su">bruno@applmat.msk.su</a>)
Wolfram Research, Inc.<br>
100 Trade Center Dr.,Suite 600<br>
Champaign, IL 61820, USA<br>
</ADDRESS>
<p>

<h3>Description</h3>

   Hamiltonian Systems of differential equations describe problems
   from Celestial Mechanics, Mathematical Physics, Hydrodynamics etc.
   Special methods of Computer Algebra were developed for these fields,
   especially for Celestial Mechanics. New achievement in applications
   of CA for studying the Hamiltonian Systems are the longtime theories
   of perturbation, the analysis of different kinds of stability,
   study of bifurcations, existence and finding new integrals etc.
   They will be interesting to a broad auditorium. On the other side,
   new achievement in other applications of Computer Algebra may
   be interesting for the specialists in Hamiltonian Systems.


